-### Edge Cases and Pitfalls
-*   **Non-manifold edges:** Two polygons may share two vertices that are not on a polygon edge [S1, unofficial]. Minimal area triangulation might introduce the same edge for both polygons, creating non-manifold edges [S1, unofficial]. By default, the code introduces an additional vertex (the plane's barycenter) to ensure a manifold mesh [S1, unofficial]. The `--nonManifold` flag disables this, potentially resulting in non-manifold edges [S1, unofficial].
-*   **Ambiguous Cases:** The original Marching Cubes algorithm has ambiguous cases where the topology is not uniquely determined by the vertex signs [S1, unofficial]. The full case table resolves these by using additional information (average value of face corners) [S1, unofficial].
